    {
      "claim": "The query is a small neutral amide (MW ~299, TPSA 42, HBD 1, logD 4.01) with a lipophilic aryl thioether/chloro/fluoro motif; the closest structural context, an 18F-labeled aryl thioether chloro/fluoro aniline series, showed excellent rat brain uptake and retention after IV injection.",
      "card_ids": ["C08"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Multiple direct in vivo CNS-exposure records for similar amide/heteroaromatic/halogenated small molecules are positive: 4NPBTA permeated the intact mouse BBB with high initial uptake and washout; compound 2 gave equivalent plasma and brain concentrations; [18F]7a showed sufficient mouse brain uptake for PET; mS-11 reached about 1 µg/g brain after IP dosing.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C07", "C03", "C09"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "New L2 records reinforce the same pattern: C29 crossed the BBB in mice after oral dosing without accumulating; [18F]7a showed whole-brain uptake with washout (SUV 0.91 at 5 min); LY450108 was quantifiable in human CSF (plasma:CSF 44:1 to 82:1) and its biarylsulfonamide class is centrally acting.",
      "card_ids": ["C05", "C11", "C15", "C16", "C04", "C14", "C17"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only negative CNS-exposure records concern 2,4-dichlorophenoxyacetic acid, an ionized carboxylic acid herbicide with restricted CNS penetration; this context has low transferability to the neutral, lipophilic query amide.",
      "card_ids": ["C12", "C13"]
    }
  ],
