      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C16", "C14", "C17"]
    },
    {
      "family": "associated_nonvoting_records",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C12", "C13"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/plasma, CSF, or PET measurement for the exact query molecule.",
    "No experimental P-gp/BCRP efflux data; efflux risk is only inferred as moderate.",
    "Deuterated fluoromethyl thioether metabolic stability and unbound brain fraction are not directly measured.",
    "LogD 4.01 is above the optimal CNS range and may lower unbound brain exposure, though it is not disqualifying."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Pass is better supported: the query is a small neutral amide with favorable passive BBB properties and multiple close positive CNS-exposure analog contexts, including direct rodent brain uptake and human CSF penetration; the new L2 records strengthen this conclusion, while the negative 2,4-D records are not transferable to this neutral lipophilic structure."
}

